# hosts.txt -- one address per line, for cluster_runtime_check.sh / cluster_spec_check.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Put one SSH-reachable host per line.  Lines starting with '#' are comments
# and are ignored, as are blank lines.  Only the first whitespace-separated
# token of each line is used as the address, so you may append a trailing
# comment after the address.
#
# The addresses must be reachable over plain SSH on the port you pass with
# -P (default 22) and the user you pass with -u (default root).  There is no
# jump-host, no shared NFS, no parallel-ssh fan-out: the collector scripts
# are piped to each node over stdin via `ssh ... 'bash -s -- -j'`.
#
# If a node is not reachable, do NOT silently delete it -- leave it in the
# list so it is explicitly counted in the report as unreachable.  Remove a
# node only when you intend to exclude it from the audit.
#
# Examples (replace these with your real nodes):
#   10.0.0.1
#   10.0.0.2
#   gpu-node-03
#   10.0.0.4   # storage-rail only
#
# --- uncomment and edit below ---
# 10.0.0.1
# 10.0.0.2
# 10.0.0.3
